### Page 1 of 1

```text
RESOLUTION NO. __________

ENTITLED: "A RESOLUTION DESIGNATING LOCAL BANKS AS DEPOSITORIES
FOR MUNICIPAL FUNDS."

WHEREAS, Wyoming Statute § 9-4-817 requires that municipalities keep their funds
deposited in national and state banks, including credit unions;

WHEREAS, in compliance with state law, the City of Cheyenne annually designates local
depositories for its funds;

WHEREAS, applications have been received from ANB, First Interstate Bank, FNBO,
Pinnacle Bank, Platte Valley Bank, US Bank, Wells Fargo Bank, and Wyoming Bank and Trust
for deposit of City funds for a period of one year beginning January 1, 2025; and

WHEREAS, the Governing Body wishes to designate these banks as depositories of City
funds upon delivery of security for the protection of the funds.

NOW, THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY
OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that ANB, First Interstate Bank, FNBO, Pinnacle Bank, Platte
Valley Bank, US Bank, Wells Fargo Bank, and Wyoming Bank and Trust are designated as
depositories of City funds.  This designation of the depositories will commence January 1, 2025
and continue for a period of one year.  No monies may be deposited by the City Treasurer except
in the designated banks.

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that the City Treasurer shall have the authority to place
investments on behalf of the City of Cheyenne in those instruments authorized pursuant to
Wyoming Statute § 9-4-831(a) and to enter into agreements with the listed depositories and
appropriate investment companies, after review by the City Attorney.

THIS RESOLUTION shall be in full force and effect from and after its passage in
accordance with the laws of the State of Wyoming.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED this _______ day of _____________________,
2023.

__________________________________________
Patrick Collins, Mayor

(SEAL)

ATTEST:

____________________________________
Kristina F. Jones, City Clerk
10:33 am, Dec 04 2024
